-- A default is worked out outside the rule or the record it is written on, where
-- that rule's inputs and that record's fields are not known (TYPICALLY-ONE-BEHAVIOUR-SPEC.md
-- W7, §4.3). A name in it that is spelled like one of them therefore means
-- whatever else is called that, when something is, and the answer would use that
-- value without a word. It is refused.

GIVETH A NUMBER
salary MEANS 50000

GIVETH A NUMBER
phi MEANS 8

-- ERROR: `salary` here is the definition above, not the input beside it
GIVEN salary IS A NUMBER
      bonus IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY (salary DIVIDED BY 10)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`total pay` MEANS salary PLUS bonus

-- ERROR: the same on a record's field
DECLARE Pay HAS
  salary IS A NUMBER
  extra IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY (salary DIVIDED BY 10)

-- No error: a name that is not an input of this rule
GIVEN base IS A NUMBER
      rate IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY (phi PLUS 1)
GIVETH A NUMBER
scaled MEANS base TIMES rate

-- No error: the default binds the name itself, so it never reaches the module's
-- scope
GIVEN base IS A NUMBER
      rate IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY (LET base BE 2 IN base TIMES phi)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`scaled by a local` MEANS base TIMES rate

-- No error: a name written with its section says which definition it means
§ `Rates`
    GIVETH A NUMBER
    wage MEANS 1000

    GIVEN wage IS A NUMBER
          tip IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY (`Rates`.wage DIVIDED BY 10)
    GIVETH A NUMBER
    `pay with tip` MEANS wage PLUS tip
